# What the restic-server form, booted as it ships, without a shell and
# without a config, must say on its console (make
# check-shellfree-restic-server; test/boot; forms/demo/test/console has
# the format). With no users, rest-server parks before it binds anything,
# and says why; with no domain, so does Caddy. make check-restic-server
# boots it with its config, and backs up to it.

seen    rs-needs-users     leash: \{"event":"down","service":"restic-server","why":"config restic-users: FileNotFound"\}
seen    caddy-needs-domain service-config: \{"event":"settings","service":"caddy","setting":"domain","why":"required"\}
seen    caddy-parked       leash: \{"event":"down","service":"caddy","why":"settings refused; service-config said why"\}
